WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.184
A variable can be given a new value later in a
program If sales first

00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:09.816
stores one thousand and then we assign fifteen
hundred to sales the variable now refers

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:15.475
to the newer value This is called reassignment It is

00:00:15.502 --> 00:00:21.265
useful because analytical values often change during
a workflow We may clean a value

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:25.975
convert its units apply a correction or replace an
old observation with a new one

00:00:27.711 --> 00:00:32.500
When you run this example compare the value printed
before the reassignment with the value

00:00:32.526 --> 00:00:37.674
printed after it Python processes the lines in order
so the point at which a

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.095
value changes matters
